DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppppmmqquuaanntt is obsolete.  All it does now is invoke ppnnmmqquuaanntt or  ppnnmmrreemmaapp.
       You  should use one of those programs in any new program, or if you are
       modifying an old program, and your program does not have to work with a
       version of Netpbm before 9.21 (January 2001).  ppppmmqquuaanntt exists only for
       name compatibility.

       ppnnmmqquuaanntt is fully backward compatible with ppppmmqquuaanntt _w_i_t_h_o_u_t  the  --mmaapp‐‐
       ffiillee  option;  ppnnmmrreemmaapp is fully backward compatible with ppppmmqquuaanntt _w_i_t_h
       the --mmaappffiillee option.

       Except with differences suggested by the  syntax  synopsis  above,  pppp‐‐
       mmqquuaanntt's function is the same as ppnnmmqquuaanntt and ppnnmmrreemmaapp.

       Before Netpbm 10.19 (November 2003), ppppmmqquuaanntt was a completely separate
       program from ppnnmmqquuaanntt, and was a bona fide PPM program.  That means  if
       you  gave  it a PGM or PBM image as input, it would process it as if it
       were PPM and generate a PPM output.  Now, since it is really a PNM pro‐
       gram, it processes PBM and PGM inputs as what they are and produces the
       same kind of output.

       Note: The reason ppppmmqquuaanntt was changed in Netpbm 10.19 is that for  some
       time  before that, ppppmmqquuaanntt had a serious bug that would have been dif‐
       ficult to fix -- it chose the wrong color set.   Maintaining  two  ver‐
       sions of the same code did not make sense.


